-- title:
--   An eighth-power bound for the dense-guard false-mass threshold
-- statement:
--   Let $n,n_A,n_B,n_C,q$ be natural numbers, let $A,B,C:\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$, and let $r$ be a band-owner record list with $|r|\le3n^2$. Use the scheduled band width $g$, dimensions $h,J$, and magnitude $M=2^{2048(\operatorname{inputBits}(n)+1)}$. Let $R$ be the global representation cap and let $F$ be the weighted false-incidence score on the physical owner products, with current modulus $q$ and the prime pool for the scheduled prime window. Then
--   $$
--   RF\le9M^8.
--   $$
--   The score uses differences $C_c-B_b-A_a$ and the pool's auxiliary moduli. This bounds the dense guard's representation-weighted threshold for arbitrary supplied array lengths and values under the stated record-count hypothesis.
